# CODEOWNERS — structural enforcement of the product-review boundary.
#
# A PR that touches ANY owned path below REQUIRES @TomDevine11's review before merge, and
# therefore cannot auto-merge. A PR that touches NONE of these paths (pure internal — tests,
# docs, most scripts, tooling, .claude, root config) can auto-merge once CI is green.
# Pair with branch protection: "Require review from Code Owners" + "Require status checks".
#
# This owns the surfaces where "user-facing" is unambiguous and a mistake is costly. The
# src/ interior (games/components/utils) is governed by Claude's own classification
# (auto-merge enabled ONLY on PRs it classifies internal) + the triviverse-reviewer subagent
# + the artefact-diff rule. For a STRICTER guarantee, uncomment the /src/ line at the bottom
# to force review on ALL app-code changes (you then also approve internal src refactors).

# Generated + source game data — the artefact-diff surface. Any change that alters what
# players see (incl. a data-pipeline change whose regenerated output differs) lands here.
